Notes for Testing
• For GET .../search, add city and minAge in Postman's Params tab rather than typing them into the URL
— Postman will build the query string automatically.
• For POST and PUT, select Body → raw → JSON and set header Content-Type: application/json.
• Watch the application console/log output while testing — each request should print the corresponding
[@PathVariable], [@RequestParam], or [@RequestBody] log line confirming which mechanism
handled it.
• Create at least one customer with city=Pune and age ≥ 25 before testing the search endpoint, so the filter
returns a non-empty result.
How to Run
1. Place the files in the package structure shown above.
2. Run mvn spring-boot:run (or run CustomerApiApplication from an IDE).
3. The API is available at http://localhost:8080/api/customers.
4. Open http://localhost:8080/h2-console and connect with JDBC URL
jdbc:h2:mem:customerdb, username sa, empty password.
5. Execute the Postman requests in order: POST (create a few customers) → GET by id → GET search →
PUT → DELETE.
